NAME
    grep - keep lines matching a pattern

SYNOPSIS
    <input> | grep [-i] [-v] [-n] <pattern>

DESCRIPTION
    Reads standard input and writes only the lines that contain <pattern>
    (a plain substring; no regular expressions). A pipeline filter.

    -i  ignore case (ASCII)
    -v  invert: print the lines that do NOT contain the pattern
    -n  prefix each printed line with its 1-based input line number

    Flags may be combined, e.g. -in, and come before the pattern.

EXAMPLES
    cat log.txt | grep ERROR
    ls /bin | grep -i cat
    cat log.txt | grep -vn WARN

SEE ALSO
    wc, head, tail, uniq, sort
